14. What is useMemo?
Usememo is a react hook used to memoize a calculated value and avoid unnecessari calculated value.
const total = useMemo(() => {
  return calculateTotal(items);
}, [items]);

15. What is useCallback?
UseCallback is a react hook used to memoize the function and avoid unnessari function recreation.
const handleAddToCart = useCallback((product) => {
  addToCart(product);
}, []);
<Product onAdd={handleAddToCart} />

16. What is context api?
Context api is used to share data between components without passing props.
const UserContext = createContext();
<UserContext.Provider value={user}>
  <Navbar />
  <Dashboard />
  <Profile />
</UserContext.Provider>

17. What is custom hook?
A custom hook is a resusable function used to share logic between components.

function useFetch(url) {
  const [data, setData] = useState(null);
  useEffect(() => {
    fetch(url)
      .then(res => res.json())
      .then(data => setData(data));
  }, [url]);
  return data;
}
// cal the custom hook
function Users() {
  const users = useFetch("/api/users");
}
function Products() {
  const products = useFetch("/api/products");
}

18. What is Redux?
Redux is a state management library we use to manage and share data between components.

19. What is Performance optimization ?
If we want to performance optimization in react application, we can avoid unnecessary re-renders and function recreation by using usemeo, usecallback, React.memo and lazy loading. 

useMemo → Value
useCallback → Function
React.memo → Component
Lazy loading → Load when needed 

20. What is Authentication?
Authtentication is used to verify the user's identity and allow them to access the application.

21. What is Protected routes ?
Protected routes are used to prevent access for unauthenticated users.

22. What is lazy loading?
Lazy loading means loading a page or component when we need it, Which helps to improve application performance.
const ProductDetails = React.lazy(() => import("./ProductDetails"));
<Suspense fallback={<p>Loading...</p>}>
  <ProductDetails />
</Suspense>

